From 424523f312d042d64b2abd8cd22701bde78f90e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 08:37:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10630/11362] Record that the queued run cannot unblock exp6844
 on its own

exp6844's supervisor outcome-credit audit pins its input to one frozen path,
results/experiment_6681_arc_post_redirect_outcomes.json, hardcoded in four places.
It is not a glob over applied receipts. So the queued cd82/r11l run can produce
level-up-credited redirects and exp6844's headroom_nonzero gate will still observe
False, because it never reads the new artifact.

Producing the evidence is necessary and not sufficient. A follow-on audit has to
name the new artifact as its source.

Recorded because the failure mode is silent. A later session sees a fresh supervised
run land, re-runs the audit, gets the same blocked verdict, and concludes the run
failed -- when the audit was simply pointed somewhere else.

Context from this hour: exp6845 returned the same shape as exp6844 -- audit machinery
complete, zero input, gate failing on zero obligations. Two consecutive artifacts,
which is a sequencing observation and not yet a milestone pattern; only 2 of the
exp68xx set show it, so it is not reported as one. Building an auditor before its
evidence exists is legitimate ordering, provided someone connects the two, which is
exactly what this note exists to make sure happens.

Not checked, and flagged as such: whether exp6845's tool-gap audit is pinned the same
way. Worth confirming before assuming a tool-loop run would unblock it.

